<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Gujarati strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "તમે" with "-ો", and English loanwords where Gujarati iOS uses them ("સેવ", "ડિલીટ").
  Gujarati has the CLDR plural forms one and other; "one" also takes 0, so each form keeps the number.
  The duration chips have no unit, because "12–24 કલાક" is longer than 7 characters: the captions name the hours.
-->
